---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="That didn't work — Field Notes"
  description="The subscribe form failed. Your address was not saved."
>
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top: 96px; padding-bottom: 96px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="mono-label">Didn't work</p>
      <h1
        style="margin: 20px 0 18px; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.028em;"
      >
        That didn't work, and your address wasn't saved.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Either the address didn't look like an address, or something on my end failed. Saying so is
        the whole point of this page: the previous version of this form returned a 404 and lost
        addresses without telling anyone, which is worse than failing loudly.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/#subscribe">Try again</a>, and if it fails twice it's me, not you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
